{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UjKgb2ahvMyH622Qv2jPa9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Next WI (process-options.md \"Unattended operation\") — the WI id the driver\n2\t# expects the coordinator to pick up next, in the docs/run-phase idiom (comment\n3\t# lines + one value on the last line). The managed BUILD branch reads it and, if\n4\t# that WI's row in docs/requirements/work-items.csv carries a BuildTier, uses it\n5\t# as the session's STARTING tier in place of the phase default (WI-126). The\n6\t# value may be a `;`-joined ordered DEV-SLICE BATCH of independent off-spine WIs\n7\t# — one session, one review round, strongest-member pin (WI-133); an\n8\t# absent/empty file, an unknown id, or an empty BuildTier = the phase default.\n9\t# The DRIVER maintains this alongside docs/status.md Next action.\n10\t# NOTE: WI-144 (the v3 campaign closer) is `active` but PAUSED — its SR-047\n11\t# critique loop has EXHAUSTED the AGENT_CRITIQUE_MAX=3 budget still\n12\t# CHANGES-REQUESTED (042/048/052; log.md 2026-07-14). Under single-ratify the\n13\t# budget failure_action pauses that WI + surfaces the block for the phase-v3\n14\t# g2-close ratification sitting (OI-12) but KEEPS the loop RUNNING on non-dependent\n15\t# work — so next-wi moves OFF WI-144 to the next actionable non-dependent unit\n16\t# (WI-144 resumes for its final build round after the sitting rules OI-12).\n17\t# 052-CRITIQUE disposition (OI-12): BUILDABLE rubric-meeting [MAJOR A4] queued\n18\t# .detail .badge 2.56:1 · [MINOR A4] focus ring 2.05:1 · [MAJOR T4] .blab overflow\n19\t# · U4/U3/U1 polish; OWNER-GATED (recurring) U5 palette taxonomy · [MAJOR T2]\n20\t# Knowledge-tab density · 3 TC-HARDEN. Recommend the sitting ratify the TC-HARDEN\n21\t# first so one final build round mechanizes contrast instead of another hand pass.\n22\t#\n23\t# NEXT: WI-147 (coordinator graceful pause). WI-146 (ratification package -\n24\t# trace.py --ratify view + the warn-first brief lint + gate-advance/reviewer-prompt\n25\t# wiring + the [g2]-authors-IF recipe line) SHIPPED 2026-07-14 (log.md). The loop\n26\t# continues the actionable owner-intake backlog in id order: WI-147 (graceful\n27\t# pause) -> WI-148 (weekday blackout) -> WI-149 (lowest-gate-first warn) -> WI-150\n28\t# (planner-assigned BuildTier) -> WI-151 (throughline pointer). WI-144 (the v3\n29\t# closer) is `active` but PAUSED - its\n30\t# SR-047 critique loop EXHAUSTED AGENT_CRITIQUE_MAX=3 still CHANGES-REQUESTED\n31\t# (042/048/052); single-ratify's budget failure_action pauses it + surfaces the\n32\t# block for the phase-v3 g2-close sitting (OI-12) but keep_nondependent KEEPS the\n33\t# loop RUNNING on non-dependent work. With the buffer gone, that non-dependent work\n34\t# IS the owner-intake backlog (WI-146…151): all hard predecessors done (WI-145, the\n35\t# 2026-07-14 sitting, is done), so the trajectory --strict check treats them as\n36\t# actionable and a NEEDS-HUMAN park would be a STALE end-state it rejects. So the\n37\t# loop proceeds through them in id order. The g2-close sitting is DUE in PARALLEL\n38\t# (rule OI-12, sequence the campaigns) - if the owner would rather the loop hold for\n39\t# it, they rule OI-12 / reorder next-wi. Research-knowledge WI-152+ is a coherent\n40\t# campaign the owner sequences at the sitting: do NOT auto-start it ahead of the\n41\t# owner-intake WIs. WI-144 resumes for its final build round after the sitting rules\n42\t# OI-12, then the full gate bar and the spine rejoins G3.\n43\tWI-147\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02b55c2d-fc4e-4165-92e0-c8c2e88ded1d","uuid":"0bc72710-2ffc-4e3b-89e3-ec12441e885a","timestamp":"2026-07-15T00:09:55.854Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\docs\\next-wi","content":"# Next WI (process-options.md \"Unattended operation\") — the WI id the driver\n# expects the coordinator to pick up next, in the docs/run-phase idiom (comment\n# lines + one v